course: dictionary
lesson: 14038
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). To pick the right one, look at the context: the other words in the sentence show which meaning fits. «The mannequin in the shop window wore a red coat.» The clues are shop window and coat, so a mannequin here is a model of a body, not a person.
explain: The same word can point to a person in an older text. «My grandmother worked as a mannequin in the 1950s, showing dresses to customers.» Grandmother is a person, so mannequin means a fashion model here. Ask yourself: is this a thing or a person?
explain: Some words also change with the setting. «The teacher showed us how to press on the manikin's chest.» A manikin is a training dummy, another name for a mannequin used in first aid. When you meet a word with several meanings, check the clues each time.
fact: A mannequin is a model of a human body, often used to show clothes in a shop window.
fact: «Mannequin» can also mean a person whose job is to model clothes, though this use is old-fashioned.
fact: In first aid lessons, a mannequin, also called a manikin, is a training dummy for practising CPR.
fact: «Stand still like a mannequin» means to stay very still, without moving at all.
fact: The «mannequin challenge» was a viral video game in 2016, where people froze still like mannequins.
exercise: «The mannequin in the window wore a blue dress.» What is a mannequin here? | A kind of fish | A person who tells jokes on stage | A type of bread | *A model of a body used to show clothes
exercise: «Ella practised CPR on a mannequin in her first aid class.» What is the mannequin used for? | Dancing in a video | Standing in a shop window | Taking photos for a magazine | *Practising first aid
exercise: Which phrase means to stay very still? | Jump up and down | *Stand still like a mannequin | Shout like a lion | Run like the wind
test: «Grandma was a mannequin when she was young, walking the catwalk in fine dresses.» What does mannequin mean here? | A model of a body in a shop window | A sleepy cat | A training dummy for first aid | *A fashion model, a person who models clothes
test: In 2016 the «mannequin challenge» was a viral video game. What did people do? | *Froze still like mannequins | Sang a song together | Drew pictures on the walls | Ran as fast as they could
exam: «The manikin lay on the floor while the children took turns to press its chest.» Which meaning fits best? | *A training dummy for practising first aid | A model of a body in a shop window | A kind of bread | A person who models clothes for a magazine
